BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:autumnal-equinox-20270923@todaycelebrates.com
DTSTAMP:20261014T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270923
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270924
SUMMARY:Autumnal Equinox
DESCRIPTION:The autumnal equinox is a moment rather than a day: the instant
  the center of the Sun crosses the plane of Earth's equator heading south\
 , which begins astronomical autumn in the Northern Hemisphere and spring s
 outh of the equator. The U.S. Naval Observatory puts the 2026 equinox at S
 eptember 23 at 00:05 Universal Time\, which is the evening of September 22
  across the United States. Its name promises equal day and night\, and tha
 t is the one thing it does not quite deliver.\n\nhttps://todaycelebrates.c
 om/holiday/autumnal-equinox/
URL;VALUE=URI:https://todaycelebrates.com/holiday/autumnal-equinox/
CATEGORIES:Nature
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CLASS:PUBLIC
SEQUENCE:0
END:VEVENT
